      "worked": "In $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle CDA$,\n$$\\begin{align*}AB&=CD &&\\text{(equal construction radii)}\\\\BC&=DA &&\\text{(equal construction radii)}\\\\AC&=CA &&\\text{(shared side)}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\triangle ABC\\cong\\triangle CDA$ by SSS congruence.\nThus $\\angle BCA=\\angle DAC$ (corresponding angles).\nThese are alternate angles on transversal $AC$, so $AD\\parallel BC$.",
